      "title": "Malicious bee-js npm Release and Swarm Desktop Releases Deliver SleepyDuck Ethereum C2 Backdoor",
      "summary": "A threat actor compromised Ethersphere's release pipeline on November 9, 2026, using maintainer and release-bot GitHub accounts to publish a malicious @ethersphere/bee-js 13.3.0 to npm and a trojanized Swarm Desktop 0.56.2 release on GitHub. The npm package gained a postinstall hook that downloads and executes remote JavaScript with full Node.js privileges, and the same loader was added to the Swarm Desktop Electron main process. The trusted-publishing workflow, which lacked branch and environment checks, published the malicious commit with valid provenance. The later stages use an Ethereum smart contract for C2 configuration, the same infrastructure Pluto Security tied to the SleepyDuck and EtherDuck Open VSX campaign, and they steal the Bee node password and wallet key before deploying a Go backdoor and ScreenConnect on macOS, Linux and Windows. Defenders should pin bee-js to 13.2.0, remove Swarm Desktop 0.56.2, rotate exposed wallet and CI credentials, and hunt for the listed domains and persistence artifacts.",
