      "report_date": "2026-11-09",
      "title": "Inside an AhsayCBS Intrusion: Hidden Webshells, a CryptoMiner, and a C2 Implant",
      "summary": "Huntress reports a months-long intrusion into an AhsayCBS backup server, exploiting CVE-2026-105133 (authentication bypass) and CVE-2026-105134 (unauthenticated remote code execution as SYSTEM) before Ahsay's hotfixes were released. The operator planted five JSP webshell families, including an image-steganography loader and a signed-API shell with download capability. Two XMRig miners were deployed, one persisted by a SYSTEM scheduled task that relaunches it every minute. A Python-based implant with a reflective DLL, configured to contact a C2 domain, was also found, along with tunneling tools, remote access software, and Defender exclusions. The operator also queried Veeam backup credentials, showing interest in backup infrastructure. Patching blocks the entry point but does not remove existing artifacts, so exposed servers should be hunted and likely re-imaged.",
