      "report_date": "2026-11-09",
      "title": "Trusted by Default: Qubole Cross-Account Access Abused in the Wild",
      "summary": "A threat actor used IAM credentials from an AWS account associated with Qubole to assume integration roles that customers had created to trust Qubole's account, operating between October 14 and October 26. The roles were assumed with valid External IDs, and in most affected environments the trust policies had no other legitimate vendor activity. Once inside, the actor enumerated resources, harvested secrets from Lambda, Secrets Manager and SSM Parameter Store, and used TruffleHog to validate discovered AWS, Entra ID and Okta credentials. The actor also downloaded S3 data opportunistically, sometimes entire buckets in a single session. Defenders should review CloudTrail for AssumeRole events from non-AWS source addresses, remove unused vendor trust, restrict trusted principals with source IP conditions, treat External IDs as non-secret, and enable S3 data event logging.",
