      "title": "Analyzing an Illegal Android Gambling App Built with Flutter",
      "summary": "Android/TinstaPorn.A!tr is a Flutter-built Android app that poses as an online clone of a Macau casino but is actually an illegal online gambling platform. Victims play slots and roulette games whose odds are rigged in the operators' favor, and the platform encourages compulsive gambling through VIP recharges, rebates, and referrals. The app pulls its configuration from hard-coded servers and then connects to game servers, using AES keys and HMAC-SHA256 signing for communication. Beyond financial loss, it collects geolocation data and phone numbers, which are sent to backend servers. The report notes that Flutter's reverse-engineering difficulty helped the malware evade analysis, though improved tooling now makes analysis much more manageable. Fortinet detects the malware as Android/TinstaPorn.A!tr and blocks the associated servers through its web filtering service.",
