      "report_date": "2026-11-09",
      "title": "On the hunt for ARTEX: understanding agentic attacks in AWS environments",
      "summary": "ARTEX is an AI-native penetration framework in which LLM agents plan and run attacks once an operator supplies a target and objective, and it has been observed in the wild against several AWS environments. Using compromised long-term IAM access keys, it searched CloudWatch logs with FilterLogEvents for financial information, file paths and secrets such as AKIA access keys and passwords. It also abused public Amazon Cognito user pools through anonymous sign-ups, token collection, and follow-on AWS resource enumeration. Datadog tied the activity to hundreds of internet-exposed ARTEX consoles, often hosted in Asia. Defenders should hunt for ARTEX user agents and suspicious IPs, look for noisy permission-denied errors and unusual credential use, and rotate or remove long-lived access keys.",
