      "summary": "Arra Ghouls is a previously unknown cybercriminal group, also tracked as Mimbrob, that shifted from attacking private users with infostealers and banking trojans to targeting organizations in Russia and Belarus from April 2026. It used spear-phishing emails from lookalike domains, with RAR and ZIP archives containing DLL droppers disguised as legitimate Chromium or Notepad++ files. The droppers check system locale settings for CIS countries and Moldova, then establish persistence through scheduled tasks. Its main backdoor, Arra RAT, written in Go, communicates with command servers and supports file transfer, exfiltration and TCP tunneling, while Havoc, RootRat, Chisel and Metasploit were also observed. Eighteen victims were identified across telecommunications, pharmaceutical manufacturing, IT, commerce and finance. Defenders should monitor scheduled task creation and suspicious HTTP traffic tied to Arra RAT.",
