      "report_date": "2026-11-09",
      "title": "BECna, or Very Malicious Affairs",
      "summary": "The PT ESC Threat Intelligence team observed mass BEC attacks against Russian organizations that used the BoryptGrab stealer, which researchers had publicly described in March 2026. The campaign is attributed to an actor the team calls VecnaHopper, which sent phishing emails in bulk, sometimes to more than 100 recipients at once, using compromised email accounts of Russian individual entrepreneurs. The infection chain relies on password-protected archives containing a legitimate Visual Studio debugger alongside a malicious DLL, enabling DLL side-loading of a C# dropper. The final payload harvests browser credentials, messenger and crypto wallet data, and files, then exfiltrates them as a ZIP archive via POST requests to C2 servers. Between May and September 2026, researchers confirmed 1256 targeted Russian organizations, with individual entrepreneurs making up 44% and banks, energy firms, and government bodies also frequently hit. Defenders should note that the targeting appears largely indiscriminate, consistent with automated spread through harvested contacts from earlier victims.",
