      "summary": "JFrog's report exposes AccuraSoftHire, a fake company whose careers site, job ads, recruiter personas and take-home coding test deliver malicious npm packages to job candidates. The operation hides a loader in a Tailwind plugin look-alike inside a take-home project, and the operator re-points the task to a new package each time npm removes one. The company's careers site also hands candidates a \"camera driver\" installer script that runs a payload, so the malware is served from the company's own website. Researchers linked the recruiter, task author and package publishers through shared email addresses and account activity. Defenders should treat any take-home that asks for a driver install as an attack, open unknown projects in VS Code restricted mode, and run take-home code in isolated environments.",
